  controlsText: "<b>Control pad</b>  (point a controller ray at a button and pull the trigger, or click with the mouse)\n\u2022  PREV / NEXT: choose the mirror to steer. It gets a glowing ring, and the light coming off it turns cyan.\n\u2022  \u25B2 \u25BC tilt it up / down,  \u25C4 \u25BA tilt it left / right. Tap = one step, hold = keep moving.\n\u2022  Centre button: COARSE (0.5\xB0 per step) or FINE (0.05\xB0). Use FINE for the last centimetre.\n\u2022  RESET MIRROR: start angle.   SHUTTER: beam on / off.   LASER: green 532 nm or invisible infrared 1064 nm.\n\u2022  UNDO: take back your last move.   IR VIEWER: shows infrared light.   NEXT LEVEL: skip ahead.   HELP: this screen.\n<b>Thumbstick:</b> hold GRIP and push the stick to tilt the selected mirror. A / X = fine, B / Y = next mirror.\n\n<b>Monitor:</b> the circle shows where the beams hit the output detector (goal: within 1 cm of the centre). Four equal bars = centred, the text says what to do next. Above it: close-ups of the irises. Left of the pad: the view from the selected mirror.\n<b>Sound:</b> beeps get higher and faster as the beam nears the centre of the next target.\n<b>Keyboard:</b> arrows tilt,  ,  .  mirror,  /  fine,  U undo,  Backspace reset,  L shutter,  K laser,  I IR,  N next level,  H help,  T beeps."
  onOpened:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  onClosed:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
